  "id": "BIT-tomcat-2026-73581",
  "summary": "Apache Tomcat: OpenSSL and OpenSSL-FFM TLS implementations ignore CRLs when certificate uses a keystore",
  "details": "Improper Check for Certificate Revocation vulnerability in Apache Tomcat. Both the OpenSSL and OpenSSL-FFM TLS implementations ignore CRLs when certificate uses a keystore.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 11.0.0 through 11.0.25, from 10.1.0 through 10.1.59, from 9.0.0 through 9.0.121.\n\n\n\nThe following versions were EOL at the time the CVE was created but are \nknown to be affected: from 8.5.0 through 8.5.100. Other unsupported versions may also be affected.\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 11.0.26, 10.1.59, 9.0.122, which fixes the issue.",
